invariant: INV-38
file: tls_write.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_writable_len counts in records of CH_TX_PT bytes whatever the
  peer's record_size_limit says, while ch_write cuts at the smaller of the
  two. Against a peer that asks for smaller records the answer's records
  no longer fit cap, and a caller's send that takes cap bytes fails and
  kills the session. The cap sweeps at limits of 63 and 200 object.

--- old
    size_t limit = record_plaintext_max(t);
    if (limit == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    size_t limit = t->peer_limit == 0 ? 0 : CH_TX_PT;
    if (limit == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
